{
  "extends": "@pithy-sh/tsconfig/base.json",
  "compilerOptions": {
    // **No `rootDir`, because this program is deliberately not rooted here (#476).** `rootDir` is a
    // constraint on emit, and every one of these programs is `noEmit` — but TypeScript still enforces
    // it, and with `paths` sending kit specifiers to `packages/` the whole subject of the program sits
    // outside `src`. Declaring one is `TS6059` on every kit file compiled. `src/program.ts` sets a
    // `rootDir` on the scratch projects it generates for the opposite reason: those name a kit module
    // as their own root, so they need one that contains it.
    // Same `paths` line as `tsconfig.client.json`, and for the same reason: kit specifiers resolve to
    // kit source, because the subject is the module graph a bundler walks (#476).
    "paths": { "@pithy-sh/*": ["../../packages/*"] },
    // Same two lines as `tsconfig.client.json`, and for the same reason: the DOM and nothing of a
    // Worker, with `types: []` so TypeScript cannot borrow the Workers types a sibling package
    // installed. A third program rather than one more import in `client.ts` because the two subjects
    // fail apart — #315's scope constants went green the moment they moved, while #419's response
    // schemas were still dragging D1 in. One program would have reported that as one red build and
    // hidden which half was broken.
    "lib": ["ES2022", "DOM", "DOM.Iterable"],
    "types": []
  },
  "include": ["src/responses.ts"]
}
